PROBE 1 — kill conditions (i)/(ii): does reduction order alone change a greedy
token stream? {AVX2, scalar} x {MXCSR inherited, MXCSR|=FTZ|DAZ} + same-arm repeat.
30 TinyStories-style prompts, 200 max_new_tokens, M7.
====================================================================
inherited MXCSR = 0x1F80  (FTZ=false DAZ=false RC=0)   <-- architectural default
simd capability = AVX2+FMA
objdump aegis-linux/target/release/aegis-linux:
  ldmxcsr/stmxcsr occurrences ............................ 0
  rcpps/rcpss/rsqrtps/rsqrtss/vrcp14*/vrsqrt14*/vrcp28* .. 0
  x87 arithmetic (f{add,mul,div,sub,ld,st} %st) .......... 0
  => every FP op in the shipped binary is an IEEE-754 correctly-rounded SSE/AVX
