SUMMARY over 30 prompts, 200 tokens:
  same arm repeated (determinism control) differed .. 0/30   <- control PASSES
  reduction order changed (AVX2 -> scalar) differed . 20/30  = 66.7%
  MXCSR FTZ|DAZ set, AVX2 path, differed ........... 0/30    <- MEASURED NULL
  MXCSR FTZ|DAZ set, scalar path, differed ......... 0/30    <- MEASURED NULL
  divergence index over the 20 divergent prompts: min=6 median=30 max=158

Semantic scale (prompt "Ben and his sister found a map"):
  avx2 [9..16] = [" tree"," with"," many"," birds","."," The"," bird"]  (len 162)
  scal [9..16] = [" tree"," with"," many"," leaves","."," Ben"," said"] (len  85)

FINDING 1: kill conditions (i) and (ii) DO NOT FIRE.
FINDING 2: the candidate's "MXCSR costs almost nothing" side deliverable is a
  MEASURED NULL. Mechanism: int8_act (ops.rs:122) re-quantizes activations to a
  255-level grid before every BitLinear, annihilating subnormal-magnitude values
  before FTZ could act. Log MXCSR for hygiene; it is not a deliverable.

====================================================================
PROBE 2 — kill condition (iii): does reduction order move a TEACHER-FORCED
continuation NLL (what aegis-eval --mc scores)? Falcon-E-1B, 8 ARC-shaped strings.
====================================================================
DETERMINISM CONTROL (nllctl.rs), one string, 5 sequential runs:
  force_scalar=false  ppl bits=0x402d50eb980abdb4  ppl=14.658047438918
  force_scalar=false  ppl bits=0x402d50eb980abdb4  ppl=14.658047438918
  force_scalar=true   ppl bits=0x402d1c57dd6fc439  ppl=14.555357856649
  force_scalar=true   ppl bits=0x402d1c57dd6fc439  ppl=14.555357856649
  force_scalar=false  ppl bits=0x402d50eb980abdb4  ppl=14.658047438918
  A==A2 true | B==B2 true | A==A3 after B ran true | A==B false
  => no harness nondeterminism, no state leakage across the toggle. Valid.

total NLL under the two reduction orders (same machine, same weights):
   i   ntok           nll_avx2         nll_scalar      abs_delta          rel
   0     15       37.589852970       37.491428288       9.842e-2     2.618e-3
   1     15       33.204064366       33.034479690       1.696e-1     5.107e-3
   2     16       37.954471843       37.576474338       3.780e-1     9.959e-3
   3     16       36.260709384       35.887430859       3.733e-1     1.029e-2
   4     14       39.072827567       38.722428249       3.504e-1     8.968e-3
   5     13       34.586046994       34.077962800       5.081e-1     1.469e-2
   6     13       33.746348832       34.097395619       3.510e-1     1.040e-2
   7     12       35.267123751       35.318158053       5.103e-2     1.447e-3
  worst |delta total-NLL| = 5.0808e-01 nats   worst relative = 1.469e-02

NOTE: two orders of magnitude LARGER than the 1e-4 per-element tolerance asserted
in aegis-core/tests/gemm_equivalence.rs:151. int8_act is the likely amplifier: a
last-ulp change flips a libm::roundf int8 level = a ~1/127 relative activation jump.

